w:shared {
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#ActualJourney> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#ActualJourney> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/dectective/profile#Journey> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#CommunicativeAct> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#CommunicativeAct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An act of telling or writing addressed to someone. Unlike crminf:I1 Argumentation (and E13, a subclass of I1 in CRMinf 1.2.1) it does NOT presuppose sincerity: the speaker's belief in the content is represented separately, if at all." .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#CommunicativeAct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E7_Activity> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#Disappearance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#Disappearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E5_Event> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#ExpectedToReturn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#ExpectedToReturn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Person whom the believer expects to come back (used only inside belief worlds)." .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#ExpectedToReturn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E21_Person> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#Impersonation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#Impersonation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Acting under a persona identified by an appellation that is not one's own." .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#Impersonation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E7_Activity> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#InvoluntaryDisappearance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#InvoluntaryDisappearance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/dectective/profile#Disappearance> .
<http://example.org/dectective/profile#Journey> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
